,["731 Buena Vista West","sight",37.768,-122.444,"","","","","","r","Former home of Graham Nash (and several owners later) Bobby McFerrin."],["1235 Masonic Ave","sight",37.7696,-122.4455,"","","","","","r","Patty Hearst hid in a Symbionese Liberation Army safe-house here."],["Sid Vicious house","sight",37.7686,-122.4456,"32 Delmar St","","","","","r","Site of Sid's non-fatal overdose after his last Sex Pistols show."],["Monastery of Perpetual Adoration","sight",37.7676,-122.4469,"771 Ashbury St","typically 6:15AM-6PM","","","","r","Monastery of cloistered nuns from the order of the Sisters of Perpetual Adoration that holds daily services as well as special masses and novenas for holidays."],["Cha-Cha-Cha","restaurant",37.7692,-122.452,"1801 Haight St","Lunch: daily 11:30AM-4PM. Dinner: Sun-Thu 5-11PM, Fri Sat 5-11:30PM","","","","r","Popular Cuban tapas place. Good sangria. Typical wait is 1–2 hours on weekends, and they don't take reservations. Great bar, always crowded with a fun 'artsy' crowd. Be warned, the sangria packs a punch!"],["Haight Street Market (aka Gus's)","restaurant",37.7702,-122.4476,"1530 Haight St","7AM-9PM daily","","","","r","Family-owned grocery store serving the Upper Haight since 1981. Well-stocked, and with a good range of organic fruit and veg. Also has a deli counter that makes a wide range of sandwiches, which can be eaten at the parklet outside."],["The DeLuxe","bar",37.7698,-122.4472,"1511 Haight St","","","","","r","This small, stylish bar has been around for a long time. It's all about freshly squeezed cocktails. Deluxe hosts jazz most nights, always by local acts. The bartenders are friendly and the crowd is arty and hip."],["Aub Zam-Zam","bar",37.7695,-122.4493,"1633 Haight St","Mon-Fri 3PM-2AM, Sat Sun 1PM-2AM","","","","r","A 1930s vintage cocktail bar with a beautifully restored arabesque art-deco decor. Written up in 'W' and 'Newsweek' magazines for the best martinis in the US back in the 80s. Drinks are moderately expensive but of exceptional quality,…"],["Gold Cane","bar",37.7697,-122.448,"1569 Haight St","","","","","r","A great place for cheap, strong drinks, and friendly bar-tenders. Divey atmosphere, local crowd. Has a pool table and small outdoor patio for smokers of all types."],["Kezar Pub & Restaurant","bar",37.7678,-122.4529,"770 Stanyan St","Mon 11:30AM-midnight, Tue-Fri 11:30AM-2AM, Sat 6AM-2AM, Sun 6AM-midnight","","","","r","A popular English-themed pub where you can watch soccer."],["Magnolia","bar",37.7704,-122.4451,"1398 Haight St","","","","","r","Serves solid food and microbrews, including some excellent cask conditioned beers."],["Trax","bar",37.77,-122.4459,"1437 Haight St","","","","","r","A gay bar for gay men and lesbians that is also very much straight-friendly. Small, divey, and a local's scene. Drinks are cheap, and on Saturday nights it offers ridiculously cheap drink specials ($1 well cocktails before 10PM)."],["Children's Playground","sight",37.7681,-122.4572,"","","","","","r","A large and unique kid's play area. Next door is a historic Carousel, which runs 10AM-4:30PM daily from Memorial Day-Labor Day and Saturdays and Sundays the rest of the year."],["Conservatory of Flowers","sight",37.772,-122.46,"100 John F Kennedy Dr","Tue–Sun 10AM–4:30PM","","","","r","This antique palatial greenhouse, one of the first structures of its kind in the county, is filled with a huge variety of beautiful and exotic plant species. Pay special attention if the Titan Arum is blooming, as it only does every few…"],["Hippie Hill","sight",37.76967,-122.45796,"","","","","","r","Near the district's eastern border is the entrance to Golden Gate Park. Walking into the park and through a small tunnel beneath the Alvord Lake Bridge, the first large field and adjacent hill are known as Hippie Hill. In dry weather,…"],["The Panhandle","sight",37.77221,-122.4477,"(between Fell and Oak, Steiner and Baker streets)","","","","","r","This long narrow park is the main entrance to Golden Gate Park, which goes for another 40+ blocks to the west (and the Pacific Ocean). The Panhandle also includes the most famous bicycle route in the city, the Wiggle, which follows the…"]]}